From: Chris <16943149+nepenth@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] Warm DSpark probabilistic rejection helper kernels

Live rc7 JIT-monitors `_compute_local_logits_stats_kernel`,
`_rejection_kernel`, and `_resample_kernel` on the first readiness
request. Those kernels live in `rejection_sample()`, which is the
probabilistic DSpark path (`draft_sample_method=probabilistic`). The
greedy `rejection_greedy_sample_kernel` warmup does not cover them.

The Triton cache on the rc7 canary has exactly two specializations per
kernel, split by `target_logits` pointer dtype (bf16 vs f32) at
BLOCK_SIZE 8192/1024 on sm121. Call `rejection_sample()` on dummy
tensors for those dtypes, with and without draft logits, at request
counts 1 and min(max_num_seqs, 4). No dummy model forward.

Do not bake this into the running rc7 image.
---
--- a/tests/model_executor/test_spec_rejection_warmup.py
+++ b/tests/model_executor/test_spec_rejection_warmup.py
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+import torch
+
+from vllm.model_executor.warmup.kernel_warmup import (
+    _DSPARK_REJECTION_HELPER_DTYPES,
+    _dspark_rejection_helper_draft_modes,
+    _dspark_rejection_helper_num_reqs,
+)
+
+
+def test_dspark_rejection_helper_warmup_covers_observed_triton_keys() -> None:
+    # Live rc7 cache: two specializations per kernel, split by target_logits
+    # pointer dtype (bf16 vs f32). Request counts match the 0028-style 1/4
+    # ladder used for DSpark padded-input warmup.
+    assert _DSPARK_REJECTION_HELPER_DTYPES == (torch.bfloat16, torch.float32)
+    assert _dspark_rejection_helper_num_reqs(6) == (1, 4)
+    assert _dspark_rejection_helper_num_reqs(1) == (1,)
+    assert _dspark_rejection_helper_num_reqs(2) == (1, 2)
+    assert _dspark_rejection_helper_draft_modes() == (False, True)
+
+
+def test_dspark_rejection_helper_warmup_rejects_empty_batch() -> None:
+    assert _dspark_rejection_helper_num_reqs(0) == (1,)
